1
00:00:00,764 --> 00:00:02,244
(Wil:)I wasn't.

2
00:00:04,701 --> 00:00:06,111
(Penny:)Me, either.

3
00:00:07,737 --> 00:00:11,117
(Leonard:)So, what do you think, is there a
professional downside to doing it?

4
00:00:11,274 --> 00:00:12,614
(Wil:)Well, it's tricky.

5
00:00:12,776 --> 00:00:15,446
(Wil:)You want to take projects
that you're excited about,

6
00:00:15,612 --> 00:00:17,892
(Wil:)but sometimes you also
have to pay the bills.

7
00:00:18,782 --> 00:00:20,522
(Wil:)When you're on the set
working on something

8
00:00:20,684 --> 00:00:24,034
(Wil:)that you just know in your heart
is bad, not Star Trek...

9
00:00:25,722 --> 00:00:28,032
Yeah, beam me up. I love it!

10
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:33,810
(Wil:)Anyway, those jobs
can be soul-crushing.

11
00:00:33,964 --> 00:00:35,704
(Penny:)That's what I'm afraid of.

12
00:00:35,865 --> 00:00:37,745
Well, I was in Stand By Ma
when I was a kid,

13
00:00:37,901 --> 00:00:39,401
(Wil:)and it was a huge success.

14
00:00:39,569 --> 00:00:42,139
(Wil:)The terrible movies I did
came after that.

15
00:00:42,305 --> 00:00:43,975
(Wil:)Imagine how that feels.

16
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:45,140
(Leonard:)Sounds rough.

17
00:00:45,308 --> 00:00:47,588
(Wil:)I'm telling you,
this business is brutal.

18
00:00:47,744 --> 00:00:50,784
(Wil:)To this day,
I hate going on auditions.

19
00:00:50,947 --> 00:00:55,327
(Wil:)Okay, I walk in, and I can just
feel them thinking,

20
00:00:55,485 --> 00:01:01,025
"He was such a cute kid.
What happened to him?"

